* ADR1399H Precision Voltage Reference Circuit
* The ADR1399 is a 7.05V precision shunt reference with a built-in heater.
* The heater is powered directly from the 15V supply.
* The Zener is biased at approximately 3mA via R1.

* Primary input supply
V1 IN 0 15

* Bias resistor for the Zener ( (15V - 7.05V) / 3mA ≈ 2.67kΩ )
R1 IN OUT 2.67k

* ADR1399 Subcircuit Instantiation
* Standard LTspice pin order: Heater+, Heater-, Zener+, Zener-
X1 IN 0 OUT 0 ADR1399

* Output bypass capacitor for noise reduction
C1 OUT 0 1u

* Light load (100kΩ draws ~70µA)
R2 OUT 0 100k

* Transient analysis to allow the heater and reference to settle
* Runs for 2 seconds, saving data only for the last 1 second to measure the settled DC output.
.tran 0 2 1

.end
